---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, COMPANY } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Legal notice" description="Company details for airworthywp.com and the Airworthy plugin.">
	<div class="wrap page-head">
		<p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
		<h1>Legal notice</h1>
	</div>
	<div class="wrap prose" style="padding-bottom: 80px;">
		<p>This website and the Airworthy plugin are provided by:</p>
		<p>
			<strong>{ COMPANY.name }</strong><br />
			Registered in Ireland, company number { COMPANY.cro }<br />
			Registered office: { COMPANY.address }<br />
			VAT number: { COMPANY.vat }<br />
			Email: <a href={ `mailto:${ SITE.email.hello }` }>{ SITE.email.hello }</a><br />
			Website: <a href={ COMPANY.url }>{ COMPANY.url.replace( 'https://', '' ) }</a>
		</p>

		<h2>Licence</h2>
		<p>The Airworthy plugin is free software, released under the GNU General Public License. It bundles open-source libraries under their own licences; see the <a href="/docs/#bundled-libraries-and-licences">list in the docs</a>.</p>

		<h2>No warranty</h2>
		<p>Airworthy helps you plan a PHP upgrade. It reads code without running it, so it can't catch every problem: some only appear when code runs with your data and settings, or come from your server's configuration or other software. Its results are guidance, not a guarantee that your site will work on a new PHP version.</p>
		<p>Before changing the PHP version of a live site, back up its files and database, try the new version on a staging copy first, and make sure you know how to switch back. You are responsible for changes made to your site and server.</p>
		<p>The plugin is free software, provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose, as set out in its licence (the GNU General Public License).</p>

		<h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
		<p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, DigitalKind Limited is not liable for any loss or damage arising from the use of Airworthy or of this website, including loss of data, revenue or business, downtime, or damage caused by changing your PHP version or by any action taken on the basis of Airworthy's results. Nothing in this notice limits or excludes any liability that cannot be limited or excluded under applicable law.</p>

		<h2>Trademarks</h2>
		<p>WordPress is a trademark of the WordPress Foundation. PHP is a trademark of the PHP Group. Airworthy is not affiliated with or endorsed by either. Plugin names mentioned on this site belong to their owners.</p>
	</div>
</Base>
